@@ -3,3 +3,20 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## API
+
+### `resolvePointer(document, pointer)`
+
+Resolves a [JSON Pointer](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6901) (RFC 6901) against a JSON document and
+returns the value it refers to.
+
+```ts
+import { resolvePointer } from 'json-toolkit';
+
+resolvePointer({ foo: ['bar', 'baz'] }, '/foo/0'); // 'bar'
+resolvePointer({ foo: ['bar', 'baz'] }, ''); // { foo: ['bar', 'baz'] }
+```
+
+Throws an error when `pointer` is not a syntactically valid JSON Pointer, or when it does not resolve to
+a value in `document` (e.g. a missing member, an out-of-bounds array index, or indexing into a scalar).
